# Plain English (Grade 9 beginner)

All **user-visible** Crowth copy must be easy for a Grade 9 English beginner.

## Rules
- Prefer short words and short sentences.
- Keep explanations to **3–5 sentences** (never long essays).
- Avoid hard finance jargon (alpha, sharpe, VaR, regime, momentum, actuarial).
- If a number helps, keep it simple (%, R amounts).
- Money display stays in **rand (R)** unless showing a conversion note.

## Where this applies
- Simple Explanation, AI Advisor replies, Home insights blurbs
- Compare tips/verdicts, onboarding, errors, empty states, badges/labels
- Worker-generated text (`actuarial`, `sentiment`, `ai`, insights predictions)

## Do not
- Dump textbook / academic wording into the UI
- Show more than 5 explanation sentences in Simple Explanation
- Use em-dashes packed with jargon

When adding or editing copy, rewrite it in plain English before shipping.
